# API Configuration
# =================
# The Next.js backend runs on port 3000 by default.
# 
# For Android Emulator:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   (10.0.2.2 is the special alias for localhost from Android emulator)
#
# For iOS Simulator / Web:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# For Physical Android Device:
#   1. Find your machine's LAN IP address:
#      - macOS/Linux: ifconfig | grep "inet " | grep -v 127.0.0.1
#      - Windows: ipconfig | findstr IPv4
#   2. Set the URL with your IP:
#      EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.100:3000
#   3. Make sure your firewall allows connections on port 3000
#   4. Your phone and computer must be on the same WiFi network
#
# For Production/Staging:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.carezoa.com

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Google Maps API Key (Android only)
# Get your key from: https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/credentials
# Enable "Maps SDK for Android" in your Google Cloud project
GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here
